<p>He split his time between working in Bismarck and developing his homestead. At the urging of his bride he started his own business, Mandan Monument Works. On July 27, 1915, he set up his shop at 522 West Main St. Area farmers would frequently select a fieldstone on their property and engage Rybnicek to carve their gravestone. The practice served to cut material costs, important during the Great Depression era. click to enlarge</p>

