<p>In 1925, Hynek was commissioned by the Daughters of the American Revolution (DAR) at the request of then Governor R. A. Nestos to carve the state's Great Seal on a three-foot by two and a half-foot piece of native granite. A total of 193 commemorative stones were donated by states, cities, organizations, individuals and foreign countries to be inset into the interior walls of the Washington Monument. North Dakota's stone, one of the very last to be installed, is located on the 350 foot elevation landing.</p>

